--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0252. The audit
(docs/audit-0252-worktree-ownership-2026-07-12.md) found erg-pr-merge's
`in_worktree()` is literally `[ -f .git ]` — the weak predicate the whole
0252 family exists to retire. erg-pr-merge mutates aggressively (ticket
close commit, push, merge), so a false "in worktree" answer is costly.
This may be acceptable if the 0296 guard already fronts every mutation
erg-pr-merge performs — in that case, document why and close.

## Relevant files

- erg-pr-merge script (locate via `which erg-pr-merge` / skills/merge)
- `scripts/` — 0296 guard, for the shared identity check

## Actions

1. Determine what in_worktree() actually gates inside erg-pr-merge and
   what goes wrong under I1/I2 conditions there.
2. Either replace the check with the 0296 identity predicate (cwd
   worktree-name segment == `basename $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)`,
   not primary root), or record in the script a comment justifying why
   the weak check is sufficient given the guard in front of it.

## Test

- If tightened: red first — `[ -f .git ]` true but rev-parse resolving
  elsewhere must make in_worktree() return false.

## Verification

- [ ] erg-pr-merge still works from a normal worktree end-to-end
- [ ] Decision (tighten vs justify) recorded in the script

## Invariants

- Merge flow behavior unchanged for the legitimate path

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Predicate tightened or justification comment merged
- [ ] `make check` passes
